WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.093 --> 00:00:14.320
It was fall at Green Gables.

2
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:19.944
Anne and Diana Barry were resting in a sunny corner of the Green Gables orchard.

3
00:00:20.685 --> 00:00:21.885
They had been picking apples.

4
00:00:21.905 --> 00:00:27.589
"It's been a nice summer," said Diana, "and Miss Lavender's wedding was the highlight.

5
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.292
Winter will be awfully dull with you and Gilbert gone."

6
00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:34.766
"Fred will be here," said Anne teasingly.

7
00:00:34.786 --> 00:00:39.309
"Still, I can't believe you leave next week!"

8
00:00:39.729 --> 00:00:41.510
said Diana for the hundredth time.

9
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.372
"I'll be so lonely."

10
00:00:43.392 --> 00:00:46.234
"It's me who'll be lonely!"

11
00:00:46.674 --> 00:00:47.314
said Anne.

12
00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:50.216
"I don't know anyone at Redmond College."

13
00:00:50.236 --> 00:00:57.281
"Except Gilbert—and Charlie Sloane," said Diana, teasing Anne the way Anne had teased her.

14
00:00:57.301 --> 00:01:04.209
"Charlie Sloane will be a great comfort," Anne said sarcastically, and they both laughed.

15
00:01:04.929 --> 00:01:07.970
Diana knew that Anne did not enjoy Charlie's attention.

16
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.631
Both girls were less sure of how Anne felt about Gilbert.

17
00:01:12.331 --> 00:01:17.292
They were great friends, but Gilbert had been expressing some romantic interest in Anne lately.

18
00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:22.614
Diana soon returned home, and Anne went to the post office.

19
00:01:24.454 --> 00:01:29.016
There she picked up a letter she'd received from Priscilla Grant, a friend that Anne had made at

20
00:01:29.056 --> 00:01:29.856
Queen's College.

21
00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:34.499
As Anne walked home, reading the letter, she bumped into Gilbert Blythe.

22
00:01:34.519 --> 00:01:38.301
"Gilbert!" Anne said excitedly, holding out the letter.

23
00:01:38.321 --> 00:01:41.784
"Priscilla Grant is going to Redmond College too!"

24
00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:46.587
"I think we'll be very happy at the college, Anne," said Gilbert.

25
00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:51.890
"I've heard Halifax is a nice old town with many beautiful parks and magnificent scenery."

26
00:01:52.951 --> 00:01:59.376
"I wonder if it will be—can be—any more beautiful than this," murmured Anne, looking around her.

27
00:02:02.128 --> 00:02:04.830
Gilbert and Anne leaned on the bridge near the old pond.

28
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:08.293
"You are very quiet, Anne," said Gilbert at last.

29
00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:11.375
He covered Anne's slender hand with his own.

30
00:02:12.376 --> 00:02:17.019
His hazel eyes grew dark, and he opened his mouth to speak of his love for Anne.

31
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.502
But Anne snatched her hand away and turned quickly.

32
00:02:20.522 --> 00:02:23.664
"I must go home!"

33
00:02:24.024 --> 00:02:24.765
she exclaimed.

34
00:02:26.046 --> 00:02:28.888
She chattered away until they parted a few minutes later.

35
00:02:30.088 --> 00:02:35.391
"I never felt glad to see Gilbert go before," she thought as she walked alone up the lane

36
00:02:35.451 --> 00:02:36.252
to Green Gables.

37
00:02:37.192 --> 00:02:40.674
"Our friendship will be spoiled if he goes on with this nonsense.

38
00:02:41.455 --> 00:02:43.716
Why can't boys just be sensible?"

39
00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:47.478
The following week went quickly.

40
00:02:48.378 --> 00:02:52.901
The Avonlea Improvement Society gave a farewell party in honor of Anne and Gilbert.

41
00:02:53.821 --> 00:03:01.287
Everyone was there: Diana Barry, rosy and dimpled, together with Fred; Jane Andrews, neat and sensible; Ruby Gillis,

42
00:03:01.427 --> 00:03:07.452
pretty with red geraniums in her golden hair; and Gilbert Blythe and Charlie Sloane, both trying to stay

43
00:03:07.492 --> 00:03:08.993
as close to Anne as possible.

44
00:03:11.015 --> 00:03:14.959
Anne enjoyed the evening tremendously, but at the end it was spoiled.

45
00:03:15.919 --> 00:03:19.482
On the veranda Gilbert tried again to say something romantic to her.

46
00:03:20.724 --> 00:03:26.504
Anne was so annoyed that later, to punish him, she decided to walk home with Charlie Sloane.

47
00:03:26.524 --> 00:03:31.725
When she looked to see if her punishment was working, Anne saw Gilbert leaving with the beautiful Ruby

48
00:03:31.765 --> 00:03:37.347
Gillis. She felt a small knot in her stomach—her punishment had backfired!

49
00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:44.969
A week later it was Monday, the day that Anne, Gilbert, and Charlie were to leave for Redmond

50
00:03:44.989 --> 00:03:48.410
College. Rain poured down, and Mrs.

51
00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:52.431
Lynde, Marilla, Dora, and Anne were quietly eating breakfast.

52
00:03:53.471 --> 00:03:59.429
For the first time ever, Davy did not eat, but instead spent the meal crying into his porridge.

53
00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:02.410
Afterwards Marilla and Mrs.

54
00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:03.950
Lynde kissed Anne good-bye.

55
00:04:04.991 --> 00:04:10.852
Dora squeezed out two tears and kissed Anne primly, but Davy refused to say good-bye at all.

56
00:04:11.632 --> 00:04:14.233
Instead he ran and hid in the cupboard.

57
00:04:15.594 --> 00:04:18.855
Diana arrived with the horse and buggy, and Anne climbed in.

58
00:04:19.115 --> 00:04:23.456
Davy's muffled cries were the last sounds Anne heard as she left Green Gables.

59
00:04:24.832 --> 00:04:29.736
When they arrived at the Avonlea train station, Charlie and Gilbert were waiting on the platform.

60
00:04:30.977 --> 00:04:35.961
Anne just had time to check her luggage, show her ticket, and say a hurried good-bye to Diana

61
00:04:36.281 --> 00:04:38.203
before the train left for Charlottetown.

62
00:04:39.864 --> 00:04:45.529
Anne, Charlie, and Gilbert got off the train at Charlottetown and boarded the ferry bound for Nova Scotia.

63
00:04:46.469 --> 00:04:51.313
As the ferry left the harbor, the sun came out, and Anne felt a little less homesick.

64
00:04:52.754 --> 00:04:57.057
Charlie became so seasick that Anne and Gilbert were left alone on the deck.

65
00:04:57.077 --> 00:05:00.258
"Oh, Gilbert," said Anne.

66
00:05:00.278 --> 00:05:05.721
"I do hope I'll like Redmond College, but I'm sure I won't!"

67
00:05:07.582 --> 00:05:08.982
"Anne, that's not like you!"

68
00:05:09.382 --> 00:05:10.783
Gilbert said, surprised.

69
00:05:10.803 --> 00:05:14.805
"I've always longed to go to college," said Anne.

70
00:05:14.825 --> 00:05:17.906
"But now that I am, I wish I wasn't!"

71
00:05:18.386 --> 00:05:19.026
She paused.

72
00:05:19.987 --> 00:05:22.268
"I'll have a good cry and then I should feel better."

73
00:05:23.996 --> 00:05:27.018
Anne walked to other end of the deck and did just that.

74
00:05:28.899 --> 00:05:33.401
It was nine o'clock that night when the boat reached Halifax, and they found themselves in the crowded

75
00:05:33.461 --> 00:05:41.185
port. Anne felt horribly bewildered, but before long Priscilla Grant, who had come to Halifax on Saturday, grabbed

76
00:05:41.225 --> 00:05:43.447
her. "Here you are, Anne!"

77
00:05:43.907 --> 00:05:45.348
said Priscilla with a smile.

78
00:05:45.368 --> 00:05:47.749
"And I suppose you're pretty tired."

79
00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:52.992
Anne exclaimed.

80
00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:58.301
"Priscilla, if you weren't here, I think I would just sit down on my suitcase and cry!"

81
00:05:59.161 --> 00:06:03.083
Priscilla smiled and said, "Is that Gilbert Blythe over there, Anne?

82
00:06:03.683 --> 00:06:04.503
He's grown up!

83
00:06:05.003 --> 00:06:06.503
And of course that's Charlie Sloane.

84
00:06:07.044 --> 00:06:08.124
He hasn't changed."

85
00:06:09.304 --> 00:06:12.865
Anne and Priscilla waved good-bye to Gilbert and Charlie and got in a cab.

86
00:06:12.885 --> 00:06:22.708
"We're staying in a lovely boardinghouse, Anne," Priscilla said, "Our landladies are lovely too—Miss Hannah Harvey and Miss

87
00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:23.508
Ada Harvey.

88
00:06:23.928 --> 00:06:24.529
They're twins."

89
00:06:24.549 --> 00:06:30.921
"I can't get away from twins," Anne said, smiling as she thought of Davy and Dora.

90
00:06:32.103 --> 00:06:36.851
Then she and Priscilla set off toward their new home and new life in Halifax.
